PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform components; no Tailwind/Recharts ported)
  PageContainer          → SwiftUI ScrollView/VStack scaffold + ViewThatFits adaptive header (macOS regular / iOS compact).
  MetricCard ×4          → TSMetricCard (Components/DataDisplay) — web `MetricCard` parity component.
  GlassPanel ×3          → TSGlassPanel (Components/UI) — native material (ADR-005).
  Recharts AreaChart     → TSAreaChart (Components/Charts, Swift Charts) — gradient area; P3 wrapper, never a WKWebView.
  Recharts BarChart      → TSBarChart (Components/Charts, Swift Charts) — bars; P3 wrapper.
  DataTable              → TSDataTable<MileagePageMonthlyRow> with 4 sortable TSColumns (Month/Distance/Drives/per-Drive).
  AlertBanner            → TSAlertBanner(tone:.danger) (Components/Feedback) on the aggregated source error.
  EmptyState             → TSEmptyState("No Entries") (ContentUnavailableView) for every empty chart/table.
  Skeleton               → TSStatSkeleton (metrics) + TSChartSkeleton (charts) on the initial fetch.
  DataFreshnessAuto      → TSFreshnessIndicator chip from the connection axis (live/stale/offline, ADR-013).
  convertDistanceFromSI  → MileagePageUnit.convert(kilometers:) (km×0.621371 for mi); SI stays on the wire / in the model.
  Charts x-axis note     → the P3 wrappers index points on the chronological bucket order; each bucket's date is carried
                           as the point id + summarized in a per-panel range caption (web date X-axis context preserved).
  i18n      : every visible string via LocalizedStringKey (component titles) or MileagePageStrings/String(localized:)
              (chart series / table headers / banner detail); web key names kept; 16 keys in Localizable.xcstrings.
  a11y      : panels .accessibilityElement(.contain), charts .accessibilityLabel(series), header combined, ≥44pt targets,
              Dynamic Type via the token ramp, light/dark + increased-contrast via the generated dynamic colors.
  telemetry : view.opened surface="MileagePage" via MileagePageModel.start (P1/S11), default OSLog sink.
  units     : formatted at the render boundary by MileagePageUnit/MileagePageFormat from the model's snapshot unit label.

